.Dd June 7, 2013
.Dt MICRODLNA.CONF \&5 "File Formats Manual"
.Os Debian
.Sh NAME
.Nm microdlna.conf
.Nd microDLNA server configuration file
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm /etc/microdlna.conf
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr microdlnad 1
reads configuration options from the system-wide configuration file
.Pa /etc/microdlna.conf ,
or the file specified with
.Fl f
on the command line. The file contains keyword-argument pairs, one per line.
Lines starting with
.Ql #
and empty lines are interpreted as comments.
.Pp
The possible
keywords and their meanings are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm album_art_names
List of filenames to check for when searching for album art cache, separated by
forward slashes
.Pq Ql / .
This option can be specified more than once.
.It Cm db_dir
Path to the directory
.Nm microdlnad
should use to store its database and album art cache.
If it is not set, no database is built: each folder is read from disk when a
client browses it. Durations, resolutions, tags and thumbnails are learned
only for small folders
.Pq see Cm probe_limit
and played files, and kept in memory.
Search, the Artist/Album/Genre views, bookmarks and TiVo support need a
database.
.It Cm enable_tivo
Support for streaming .jpg and .mp3 files to a TiVo supporting HMO. Set to
.Dq yes
to enable support for streaming JPEG and mp3 files to a TiVo supporting HMO.
Set to
.Dq no
(default) otherwise.
.It Cm friendly_name
Customize the name that the
.Nm microdlnad
server sends to clients. Defaults to
.Dq hostname:\ username .
.It Cm force_sort_criteria
Always set SortCriteria to this value, regardless of the SortCriteria passed by the clien
t. ( E.g. force_sort_criteria=+upnp:class,+upnp:originalTrackNumber,+dc:title )
.It Cm inotify
Set to
.Dq yes
to enable inotify monitoring of the files under
.Cm media_dir
to automatically discover new files. Set to
.Dq no
to disable inotify. This is the default, and it has no effect when
.Cm db_dir
is empty.
.It Cm network_interface
Comma separated list of network interfaces to bind to. Default is empty which means bind to all.
.It Cm log_dir
Path to the directory where the log file should be stored. Defaults to
.Pa /var/log/microdlna .
Not used when "systemd" mode is activated with -S switch.
.It Cm log_level
Defines the type of messages that should be logged, and down to which level of
importance they should be considered.
.Pp
The possible types are
.Dq artwork ,
.Dq database ,
.Dq general ,
.Dq http ,
.Dq inotify ,
.Dq metadata ,
.Dq scanner ,
.Dq ssdp
and
.Dq tivo .
.Pp
The levels are
.Dq off ,
.Dq fatal ,
.Dq error ,
.Dq warn ,
.Dq info
and
.Dq debug ,
listed here in order of decreasing importance.
.Dq off
turns off logging messages entirely,
.Dq fatal
logs the most critical messages only, and so on down to
.Dq debug
that logs every single messages.
.Pp
The types are comma-separated, followed by an equal sign
.Pq Ql = ,
followed by a level that applies to the preceding types. This can be repeated,
separating each of these constructs with a comma.
.Pp
Defaults to
.Dq general,\:artwork,\:database,\:inotify,\:scanner,\:metadata,\:http,\:\
ssdp,\:tivo=warn
which logs every type of message at the
.Dq warn
level.
.It Cm max_connections
Specify maximum number of simultaneous connections. Note: many clients open several simultaneous connections while streaming.
.It Cm media_dir
Path to the directory containing the media files the
.Nm microdlnad
server should share. Use this option several times if you have more than one
directory to share. To restrict a path to one specific media type, you can use
the following syntax: the letter
.Ql A ,
.Ql V
or
.Ql P ,
followed by a comma
.Pq Ql \&,
followed by the path. The meaning of the first letter is as follows:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent -compact
.It
.Ql A
for audio files;
.It
.Ql V
for video files;
.It
.Ql P
for image files.
.El
.Lp
For example, if you want to include only video files located
in /srv/multimedia/videos directory, and only music
in /srv/multimedia/music, then you would use
       media_dir=V,/srv/multimedia/videos
       media_dir=A,/srv/multimedia/music
.Lp
Another example would be
       media_dir=V,/srv/multimedia/videos
       media_dir=V,/srv/multimedia/movies
       media_dir=A,/srv/multimedia/music
.Lp
Or, if you did not care what type it finds, then you could use
       media_dir=/srv/multimedia/videos
       media_dir=/srv/multimedia/movies
       media_dir=/srv/multimedia/music
.Lp
You can mix it up, find anything in music, but only Videos, in videos and movies
       media_dir=V,/srv/multimedia/videos
       media_dir=V,/srv/multimedia/movies
       media_dir=/srv/multimedia/music
.fi
.It Cm merge_media_dirs
Merge all media_dir base contents into the root container. The default value is no.
.It Cm minissdpdsocket
Path to the MiniSSDPd socket, if you want to use
.Nm microdlnad
together with MiniSSDPd. Defaults to
.Pa /run/minissdpd.sock .
.It Cm model_name
Set the model name reported to clients.
Defaults to
.Dq Windows Media Connect compatible (microDLNA) .
.It Cm model_number
Set the model number reported to clients. Defaults to the version number of
.Nm microdlnad .
.It Cm network_interface
Network interface(s) to bind to
.Pq e.g. eth0 ,
comma delimited. This option can be specified more than once. If unspecified or empty,
.Nm microdlnad
binds to all the valid network interfaces
.Pq except loopback .
.It Cm notify_interval
Set the notify interval, in seconds. The default is 895 seconds.
.It Cm port
Port number for HTTP traffic
.Pq descriptions, SOAP, media transfer .
A port set here or on the command line
.Pq Fl p , Fl -port
is used exactly, and
.Nm microdlnad
exits if it is in use. Without one, the first free port from 8200 upwards is
used; clients find the server through SSDP discovery whatever its port.
Instances not on 8200 also get a UUID and a default
.Cm friendly_name
that include the port, so clients see them as separate servers.
.It Cm sort_transliteration
Without
.Cm db_dir :
how names are transliterated for sorting (folders first, then a natural sort,
so ep2 comes before ep10).
.Dq pinyin
(the default) gives Chinese its context-aware pinyin from
.Cm pinyin_dict
and treats everything else like
.Dq unidecode ;
.Dq icu
uses ICU's transliterator and is several times slower;
.Dq unidecode
sorts like Python natsorted(key=unidecode(t).lower()). Keys are cached, so
each name is transliterated once.
.It Cm pinyin_dict
The gzipped dictionary of
.Cm sort_transliteration Ns = Ns Dq pinyin ,
by default
.Pa /usr/share/microdlna/pinyin-dict.txt.gz .
.It Cm probe_limit
Without
.Cm db_dir :
a folder with at most this many media files
.Pq default 30
has them probed (duration, resolution, DLNA profile, tags) while the client
waits; larger folders are not. Played files are always probed in the
background, and opened folders remember their number of entries. 0 disables
probing while browsing.
.It Cm probe_time
Without
.Cm db_dir :
the longest a browse waits for probing, in milliseconds
.Pq default 500 .
Whatever isn't done by then is finished in the background and shows the next
time the folder is opened. Waiting is limited to a tenth of the time overall,
so a burst of browses (VLC opens every subfolder of the folder it shows) never
stalls the server.
.It Cm presentation_url
Define the URL presented to clients
.Pq e.g. Dq http://example.com:80 .
The default is
.Ql / .
.It Cm root_container
Use a different container as the root of the tree exposed to clients. The
possible values 
.Bl -bullet -offset indent -compact
.It
.Ql \&.
to use the standard container;
.It
.Ql B
to use the
.Dq Browse Directory
container (this is the default);
.It
.Ql M
to use the
.Dq Music
container;
.It
.Ql V
to use the
.Dq Video
container;
.It
.Ql P
to use the
.Dq Pictures
container.
.El
If you specify
.Ql B
and the client device is audio only, then
.Dq Music/Folders
will be used as the root container.
Ignored when
.Cm db_dir
is empty: the root is then always the folder tree.
.It Cm serial
Set the serial number reported to clients. Defaults to MAC address od network interface.
.It Cm strict_dlna
Set to
.Dq yes
to strictly adhere to DLNA standards. This will allow server-side downscaling
of very large JPEG images, which may hurt JPEG serving performance on (at
least) Sony DLNA products. Set to
.Dq no
otherwise.
.It Cm tivo_discovery
Which method to use for registering in TiVo. By default
.Dq bonjour
is used. You can switch to legacy
.Dq beacon
method.
.It Cm user
Specify the user name or UID to switch to after starting. Empty (the
default) keeps running as the user that started
.Nm microdlnad :
the invoking user when run directly, or root when started by
.Pa microdlna.service
or
.Pa /etc/init.d/microdlna .
An ordinary user that cannot write the default log and pid locations gets
per-user ones under
.Ev XDG_STATE_HOME
(or
.Pa ~/.local/state )
and
.Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR .
.It Cm video_extensions , Cm audio_extensions , Cm image_extensions
File extensions served as video, audio and pictures, matched
case-insensitively and separated by
.Ql /
or
.Ql \&, .
Setting one replaces its whole list; an empty value keeps the default:
.Bl -tag -width "video:" -compact
.It video:
mpg/\:mpeg/\:avi/\:divx/\:xvid/\:asf/\:wmv/\:mp4/\:m4v/\:mts/\:m2ts/\:m2t/\:ts/\:vob/\:mkv/\:webm/\:flv/\:mov/\:3gp/\:rm/\:rmvb
.It audio:
mp3/\:flac/\:fla/\:flc/\:wma/\:asf/\:m4a/\:m4b/\:aac/\:mp4/\:m4p/\:wav/\:ogg/\:opus/\:mka/\:pcm/\:3gp/\:dsf/\:dff
.It image:
jpg/jpeg/png/webp
.El
Extensions without a built-in tag reader are probed with libavformat.
Pictures other than JPEG are served as they are, without resized versions.
.It Cm uuid
Specify device's UPnP UUID microdlna should use. By default MAC address is used to build uniq UUID.
.It Cm wide_links
Set to
.Dq no
to hide symlinks that point outside user-defined
.Cm media_dir.
By default
.Pq Dq yes ,
wide symlinks are followed.
.It Cm enable_subtitles
Set to
.Dq no
to disable subtitles support for unknown clients.
.It Cm enable_thumbnail
Set to
.Dq yes
to enable thumbnails generation for video files.  To use this option, thumbnail generation must be enable at compile time. See the following options to set thumbnails parameters.
When
.Cm db_dir
is empty this defaults to
.Dq yes ,
and only played videos and videos in small folders get a thumbnail, made in
the background and kept in memory.
.It Cm thumbnail_width
The width of the thumbnail image in pixels. Large images takes more time to generate. The default width is 160.
.It Cm thumbnail_quality
Thumbnail Image quality. The default value is 8.
.It Cm enable_thumbnail_filmstrip
Set to
.Dq yes
to make thumbnails have a film strip.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/microdlna.conf
System-wide default configuration file.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr microdlnad 8
